WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:02.040
SPEAKER: As a
developer, you want

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:04.650
to quickly deliver
great cloud applications

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:08.340
like web apps, mobile
APIs, and background jobs.

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:11.850
But choosing a cloud solution
often comes with trade-offs.

00:00:11.850 --> 00:00:14.920
On the one hand, you can
choose to manage your servers.

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:17.130
But this can mean provisioning
and configuring them

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:20.370
yourself, plus worrying about
scaling as traffic patterns

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:21.270
change.

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:24.390
And you might run the risk
of overprovisioning resources

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:26.947
and paying for more
than what you need.

00:00:26.947 --> 00:00:29.280
On the other hand, you can
pick a traditional serverless

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:30.390
solution.

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:32.850
But this can limit the
languages and libraries

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:35.550
you can use and may
require code changes

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:38.558
and make it harder to
move your application.

00:00:38.558 --> 00:00:40.350
What if you didn't have
to make that choice

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:43.110
and could enjoy the
best of both worlds?

00:00:43.110 --> 00:00:46.470
Introducing Cloud Run--
bringing server agility

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:48.720
to your containerized apps.

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:53.560
You can use Cloud Run to deploy
any stateless HTTP container.

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:56.070
This lets you write your code
in your favorite language

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:59.980
with the framework or binary
library that works for you.

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:02.850
Then simply specify the
language, your dependencies,

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:05.550
and your start script
in a Dockerfile

00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:08.910
and, with one command,
package it up into a container

00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:11.370
and boom, you're good to go.

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:14.400
Your app is now deployed
and running in the cloud.

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:16.530
You can forget about
provisioning or managing

00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:17.190
servers.

00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:19.260
Cloud Run does that for you.

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:21.900
Cloud Run automatically
and quickly scales

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:24.660
up or down based on
your incoming traffic

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:27.000
and even scales down to zero.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:30.270
And you pay only for the
resources that your app uses,

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:33.870
billed down to the nearest
one hundredth millisecond.

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:36.480
And because Cloud Run
is built with Knative,

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:40.200
you can use it with your own
Kubernetes engine cluster too.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:43.320
With Cloud Run on GKE,
you can build and deploy

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:45.450
apps to your own
Kubernetes cluster

00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:48.330
with the same easy
experience and benefits.

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:51.110
So the next time you want to
build a great app quickly,

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:52.680
check out Cloud Run.

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:54.800
Get started today.

